{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L = 1, diagonal twist: Baxter, the SoV basis, and the scalar-product determinant\n\nOne site, rep `lambda = {2,1,0}` (adjoint), inhomogeneity `theta[1]`, **diagonal** twist `K = diag(z1,z2,z3)`. Everything is exact and symbolic in `u, theta[1], h, z1, z2, z3`.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Shifts: `f^{[2n]}(u) = f(u + n h)`, and `D f(u) = f(u+h)`, so `D^{-1} f(u) = f(u-h)`.\n- Lax / monodromy `T_ij(u) = (u-theta[1]) delta_ij - h E_ji`.\n- Quantum minors `qmin_{I,K}(u) = sum_sigma sgn(sigma) prod_k T_{I_sigma(k), K_k}(u - (k-1)h)`.\n- Twisted fused transfer matrices `T_{a,1}(u) = sum_{|I|=a} z_I qmin_{I,I}(u)`, `z_I = prod_{i in I} z_i`.\n- `nu_i(u) = u - theta[1] - h lambda_i`, so `nu_1 = u-theta-2h`, `nu_2 = u-theta-h`, `nu_3 = u-theta`.\n\n## The Baxter operators\n\n$$\\mathcal O \\;=\\; 1 - \\frac{T_{1,1}(u)}{\\nu_1(u)}\\mathcal D^{-1} + \\frac{T_{2,1}(u)}{\\nu_1(u)\\nu_1^{[-2]}(u)}\\mathcal D^{-2} - \\frac{T_{3,1}(u)}{\\nu_1(u)\\nu_1^{[-2]}(u)\\nu_1^{[-4]}(u)}\\mathcal D^{-3}$$\n\n$$\\mathcal O^\\dagger \\;=\\; 1 - \\frac{T^{[2]}_{1,1}(u)}{\\nu_3^{[2]}(u)}\\mathcal D + \\frac{T^{[4]}_{2,1}(u)}{\\nu_3^{[2]}(u)\\nu_3^{[4]}(u)}\\mathcal D^{2} - \\frac{T^{[6]}_{3,1}(u)}{\\nu_3^{[2]}(u)\\nu_3^{[4]}(u)\\nu_3^{[6]}(u)}\\mathcal D^{3}$$\n\nacting as `O qhat_i^{[2]}(u) = 0` and `O^dagger qhat^j(u) = 0`.\n\n## The wave function\n\nSeparated variables sit at `x_ab = theta[1] + n_ab h`, labelled `{{n21},{n11,n12}}`, and\n\n$$\\Psi(\\{x_{21}\\},\\{x_{11},x_{12}\\}) \\;=\\; Q_1(x_{21})\\Big[Q_1(x_{11})Q_2(x_{12}-h) - Q_2(x_{11})Q_1(x_{12}-h)\\Big].$$\n\n## Contents\n\n1. Chain, Baxter operators, vacuum eigenvalues, and the GT / SoV dictionary (cells 2-8).\n2. Companion conventions: the rescaled Lax, the fused transfer matrices, the SoV covector basis (cells 10-12).\n3. The vacuum `Q`-functions from the linear difference equation for the polynomial part (cells 13-15).\n4. `<x|Psi>` against the wave function (cell 17).\n5. The abstract `3x3` scalar-product determinant expanded into wave functions (cells 19-21).\n6. Charge conservation of the measure, from a grading (cell 23).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 0. gl(N) generators in the Gelfand-Tsetlin basis, ported verbatim from SU4_L1.wb (rank-independent). ---- *)\nClearAll[ps, dim, J0, Jp, Jm, JJ, v];\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #] & /@ (Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]))},\n   If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse@Sort@res, Reverse@Sort@Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n   k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n   l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n   l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n   l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n   l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nGrid[{\n  {\"dim [2,1,0]\", dim[{2, 1, 0}]},\n  {\"GT patterns (in basis order)\", Column[ps[{{2, 1, 0}}]]},\n  {\"weights of the basis vectors\", Transpose[Table[Diagonal[JJ[i, i, {2, 1, 0}]], {i, 3}]]},\n  {\"gl(3) commutation relations hold\", And @@ Flatten@Table[JJ[a, b, {2, 1, 0}] . JJ[c, d, {2, 1, 0}] - JJ[c, d, {2, 1, 0}] . JJ[a, b, {2, 1, 0}] === KroneckerDelta[b, c] JJ[a, d, {2, 1, 0}] - KroneckerDelta[d, a] JJ[c, b, {2, 1, 0}], {a, 3}, {b, 3}, {c, 3}, {d, 3}]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
