   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 9. Q_k = z_k^{u/h} P(u): the Baxter equation reduces to a LINEAR difference equation for P. ---- *)\n(* Substituting Q(u) = zk^{u/h} P(u) into OpOpoly and dividing by zk^{u/h} gives redBax:\n   Q(u+nh) = zk^n zk^{u/h} P(u+nh), so each term just picks up a power of zk. *)\nClearAll[redBax, degMax, cc, Ppoly, res, eqs, sol, solSpace];\nredBax[zk_, Pf_][xx_] := Expand[\n   zk nu1[xx] nu1[xx - h] nu1[xx - 2 h] Pf[xx + h]\n   - (T1v /. u -> xx) nu1[xx - h] nu1[xx - 2 h] Pf[xx]\n   + (T2v /. u -> xx) nu1[xx - 2 h] Pf[xx - h]/zk\n   - (T3v /. u -> xx) Pf[xx - 2 h]/zk^2];\ndegMax = 4;\nPpoly[xx_] := Sum[cc[m] xx^m, {m, 0, degMax}];\nres = Together[redBax[z2, Ppoly][u]];\neqs = Thread[CoefficientList[Collect[Numerator[res], u], u] == 0];\nsol = Solve[eqs, Array[cc, degMax + 1, 0]];\nsolSpace = If[sol === {}, \"NO SOLUTION\", Simplify[Ppoly[u] /. First[sol]]];\nGrid[{\n  {\"redBax validated: Q_1 = z1^{u/h} means P = 1, zk = z1\", Simplify[redBax[z1, Function[y, 1]][u]] === 0},\n  {\"reduced equation for P (degree of the residual in u)\", Max[Exponent[Numerator[res], u]]},\n  {\"number of linear equations for the cc[m]\", Length[eqs]},\n  {\"general polynomial solution, degMax = 4\", solSpace},\n  {\"free parameters left\", Length[Union@Cases[solSpace, cc[_], Infinity]]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \"solve\" variables.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
