an></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.6em;\"></span><span style=\"width:0.875em;height:3.600em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.875em\" height=\"3.600em\" viewBox=\"0 0 875 3600\"><path d=\"M76,0c-16.7,0,-25,3,-25,9c0,2,2,6.3,6,13c21.3,28.7,42.3,60.3,\n63,95c96.7,156.7,172.8,332.5,228.5,527.5c55.7,195,92.8,416.5,111.5,664.5\nc11.3,139.3,17,290.7,17,454c0,28,1.7,43,3.3,45l0,9\nc-3,4,-3.3,16.7,-3.3,38c0,162,-5.7,313.7,-17,455c-18.7,248,-55.8,469.3,-111.5,664\nc-55.7,194.7,-131.8,370.3,-228.5,527c-20.7,34.7,-41.7,66.3,-63,95c-2,3.3,-4,7,-6,11\nc0,7.3,5.7,11,17,11c0,0,11,0,11,0c9.3,0,14.3,-0.3,15,-1c5.3,-5.3,10.3,-11,15,-17\nc242.7,-294.7,395.3,-681.7,458,-1161c21.3,-164.7,33.3,-350.7,36,-558\nl0,-144c-2,-159.3,-10,-310.7,-24,-454c-53.3,-528,-210,-949.7,\n-470,-1265c-4.7,-6,-9.7,-11.7,-15,-17c-0.7,-0.7,-6.7,-1,-18,-1z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.755em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.01em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.755em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.255em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.255em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.255em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.51em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.255em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.755em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[114]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{parameters} & \\left\\{\\mathrm{th}\\to \\frac{1}{3},h\\to 1,z1\\to \\frac{5}{2},z2\\to \\frac{7}{3},z3\\to \\frac{1}{6}\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{residuals, k = 1,2,3 at u = 2/7, -3/5, 11/4} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{all vanish} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "fdb333ba-7849-4e67-ae68-602fa4349caa"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. The vacuum Q-functions\n\nWriting `Q_k(u) = z_k^{u/h} P_k(u)` and dividing the Baxter equation by `z_k^{u/h}` sends `Q(u+nh) -> z_k^n P(u+nh)`, so it becomes a **linear** difference equation for `P` (`redBax`, cell 13):\n\n$$z_k\\,\\nu_1\\nu_1^{[-2]}\\nu_1^{[-4]}\\,P^{[2]} \\;-\\; T_{1,1}\\,\\nu_1^{[-2]}\\nu_1^{[-4]}\\,P \\;+\\; \\frac{T_{2,1}}{z_k}\\,\\nu_1^{[-4]}\\,P^{[-2]} \\;-\\; \\frac{T_{3,1}}{z_k^2}\\,P^{[-4]} \\;=\\; 0 .$$\n\nWith the vacuum eigenvalues of cell 5 substituted, the coefficients of `u^0 ... u^6` give 7 linear equations for the coefficients of `P`. Searching up to degree 4 the solution is unique up to normalisation in each case, with\n\n$$\\deg P_k \\;=\\; \\lambda_1 - \\mu_k \\;=\\; 2 - \\mu_k, \\qquad \\mu = (2,1,0) \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\deg P_k = 0,\\,1,\\,2 .$$\n\nMonic:\n\n$$P_1(u) = 1,\\qquad P_2(u) = u - \\frac{z_1(\\theta_1+h) - z_2(\\theta_1+2h)}{z_1-z_2},$$\n\n$$P_3(u) = (\\theta_1-u)^2 + \\frac{h\\,(\\theta_1-u)\\,(z_1+2z_2-3z_3)\\,z_3}{(z_1-z_3)(z_3-z_2)} + \\frac{h^2\\,(z_1^2 z_2 - 3 z_1 z_2 z_3 + 2 z_3^3)}{(z_1-z_3)^2 (z_3-z_2)} .$$\n\n`P_1 = 1` recovers `Q_1 = z_1^{u/h}` of cell 6. The single root of `P_2` degenerates to `theta_1+h` as `z_2 -> 0` and to `theta_1+2h` as `z_1 -> 0`, i.e. onto the zeros of `nu_2` and `nu_1`.\n\n**Verification.** Cell 14 checks `redBax = 0` symbolically for all three. Cell 15 is an *independent* check that does not reuse `redBax`: the full `Q_k = z_k^{u/h}P_k` is fed back into the Baxter equation assembled directly from the transfer matrices, at random rational `theta_1, h, z_1, z_2, z_3` and three values of `u`. All nine residuals vanish exactly.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 12. <x|Psi> vs the wave function, vacuum state. ---- *)\n(* Separated variables sit at x_ab = theta[1] + n_ab h, so Q_k(theta1 + n h) = z_k^{theta1/h} z_k^n P_k(theta1 + n h).\n   Every term of Psi carries exactly two Q_1 and one Q_2, so the common z^{theta1/h} cancels in the\n   ratio and we may work with the reduced Qred[k][n] = z_k^n P_k(theta1 + n h). *)\nClearAll[Qred, PsiWF, lhsX, rhsWF, xvFree];\nQred[k_][n_] := {z1, z2, z3}[[k]]^n (PP[k] /. u -> th + n h);\n(* Psi({n21},{n11,n12}) = Q_1(x21) [ Q_1(x11) Q_2(x12 - h) - Q_2(x11) Q_1(x12 - h) ] *)\nPsiWF[{{a_}, {b_, c_}}] := Qred[1][a] (Qred[1][b] Qred[2][c - 1] - Qred[2][b] Qred[1][c - 1]);\nlhsX = Table[Simplify[First[(x[g] /. bridge) . PsiVac]], {g, gtpats}];\nrhsWF = Table[Simplify[PsiWF[g]/PsiWF[{{1}, {0, 0}}]], {g, gtpats}];\n(* the generic pseudovacuum components xv[2..8] must drop out, since Psi_vac is the first basis vector *)\nxvFree = Union@Cases[lhsX, xv[_], Infinity];\nGrid[Join[\n  {{\"GT label {{n21},{n11,n12}}\", \"<x|Psi>\", \"Psi(n)/Psi({1},{0,0})\", \"equal\"}},\n  Table[{gtpats[[k]], lhsX[[k]], rhsWF[[k]], Simplify[lhsX[[k]] - rhsWF[[k]]] === 0}, {k, Length[gtpats]}],\n  {{\"ALL EIGHT MATCH\", Simplify[lhsX - rhsWF] === ConstantArray[0, Length[gtpats]], SpanFromLeft, SpanFromLeft}},\n  {{\"xv[i] surviving in <x|Psi> (must be none)\", xvFree, SpanFromLeft, SpanFromLeft}}\n  ], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
