   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. `<x|Psi>` matches the wave function\n\nFor the vacuum state, with separated variables at `x_ab = theta[1] + n_ab h`,\n\n$$\\big\\langle x_{\\{\\{n_{21}\\},\\{n_{11},n_{12}\\}\\}}\\,\\big|\\,\\Psi\\big\\rangle \\;=\\; \\frac{\\Psi(\\{n_{21}\\},\\{n_{11},n_{12}\\})}{\\Psi(\\{1\\},\\{0,0\\})},\\qquad \\Psi = Q_1(x_{21})\\Big[Q_1(x_{11})Q_2(x_{12}-h) - Q_2(x_{11})Q_1(x_{12}-h)\\Big]$$\n\nholds **exactly, for all eight Gelfand-Tsetlin labels**, symbolically in `theta[1], h, z1, z2, z3`. The `Q`'s are the ones constructed in cell 14, `Q_1 = z_1^{u/h}` and `Q_2 = z_2^{u/h}P_2(u)`.\n\n| `{{n21},{n11,n12}}` | `<x|Psi>` |\n|---|---|\n| `{{1},{0,0}}` | `1` |\n| `{{1},{1,0}}` | `z1 + z2/2` |\n| `{{1},{1,1}}` | `z1 z2/2` |\n| `{{2},{0,0}}` | `z1` |\n| `{{2},{1,0}}` | `z1(2 z1 + z2)/2` |\n| `{{2},{1,1}}` | `z1^2 z2/2` |\n| `{{2},{2,0}}` | `z1^2(2 z1 + z2)/2` |\n| `{{2},{2,1}}` | `z1^3 z2/2` |\n\nTwo things are visible in the table and both are checks on the construction:\n\n- **`theta[1]` and `h` drop out completely.** The overlaps are pure functions of the twist.\n- **The `n21` dependence factorises as `z1^{n21}`**, exactly as the `Q_1(x_{21})` prefactor of `Psi` demands: every `{{2},{b,c}}` entry is `z1` times the corresponding `{{1},{b,c}}` entry.\n\nThe generic pseudovacuum components `xv[2],...,xv[8]` cancel out of `<x|Psi>` entirely (`xvFree = {}`), as they must: `Psi_vac` is the first Gelfand-Tsetlin basis vector, so only `xv[1]` enters and it is removed by the normalisation `<x_vac|Psi> = 1`. This also means the match above does **not** test the generic pseudovacuum — that will only be probed once the other seven states are built.\n\n**Open.** Diagonalize the full twisted transfer matrix and build the remaining seven states, each normalised by `<x_vac|Psi> = 1` with its own `Q_2, Q_3` from the cell-13 linear equation, then re-test `<x|Psi>` on those states, where the generic pseudovacuum genuinely matters.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 13. The abstract 3x3 SoV determinant and the two wave functions, all Q abstract. ---- *)\n(* Measure M = mu/nu_1 = 1/(nu_1 nu_2 nu_3), three simple poles at theta[1] + n h, n = 0,1,2.\n   au[i,n] = Q_i(theta1 + n h) (direct), ad[j,n] = Q^j(theta1 + n h) (dual), both undetermined.\n   Columns G_1 = -Q^j Q_i, G_2 = Q^j Q_i^{[-2]}, G_3 = Q^{j[2]} Q_i against w' = (Dc_1, a_1, a_2). *)\nClearAll[Mmeas, mPoles, mW, au, ad, gvecA, rowA, detA, trG, allIJ, PsiBa, PsiAa, cube];\nMmeas[w_] := 1/(nu1[w] nu2[w] nu3[w]);\nmPoles = th + h Range[0, 2];\nmW = Table[Together[Residue[Mmeas[w], {w, p}]], {p, mPoles}];\ngvecA[{i_, j_}, n_] := {-ad[j, n] au[i, n], ad[j, n] au[i, n - 1], ad[j, n + 1] au[i, n]};\nrowA[{i_, j_}] := Sum[mW[[n + 1]] gvecA[{i, j}, n], {n, 0, 2}];\ndetA[tr_] := Expand[Det[rowA /@ tr]];\n(* the row triple is forced: each row supplies one Q_i and one Q^j, and Psi needs content {1,1,2} on both sides *)\nallIJ = Tuples[Range[3], 2];\ntrG = Select[Subsets[allIJ, {3}], Sort[#[[All, 1]]] === {1, 1, 2} && Sort[#[[All, 2]]] === {1, 1, 2} &];\n(* right wave function, in the convention verified against <x|Psi> in cell 17;\n   left wave function is the mirror, Q_i -> Q^i and -h -> +h *)\nPsiBa[{a_, b_, c_}] := au[1, a] (au[1, b] au[2, c - 1] - au[2, b] au[1, c - 1]);\nPsiAa[{a_, b_, c_}] := ad[1, a] (ad[1, b] ad[2, c + 1] - ad[2, b] ad[1, c + 1]);\ncube = Tuples[{0, 1, 2}, 3];\nGrid[{\n  {\"poles of M\", mPoles},\n  {\"residue weights\", mW},\n  {\"direct sample points n, from the residues\", Union@Cases[rowA /@ allIJ, au[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]},\n  {\"dual sample points n, from the residues\", Union@Cases[rowA /@ allIJ, ad[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]},\n  {\"direct sample points n, from Psi_B over all ns\", Union@Cases[PsiBa /@ cube, au[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]},\n  {\"dual sample points n, from Psi_A over all ms\", Union@Cases[PsiAa /@ cube, ad[_, n_] :> n, Infinity]},\n  {\"row triples with the right Q-content (unique)\", trG},\n  {\"row (1,1)\", MatrixForm[rowA[{1, 1}]]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"639560\" data-output-id=\"77\" data-out-n=\"134\" data-sub-idx=\"16\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"18\" data-sub-start=\"19\" data-sub-end=\"28\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[134]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"10\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:15.699em;vertical-align:-7.5795em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.1195em;\"><span style=\"top:-10.0795em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:10.0795em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:15.659em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-7.5795em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.0795em;\"><span style=\"top:-13.109em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">poles of M</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-11.899em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">residue weights</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.699em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">direct sample points n, from the residues</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.499em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dual sample points n, from the residues</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.299em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">direct sample points n, from Psi_B over all ns</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.099em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dual sample points n, from Psi_A over all ms</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.889em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">row triples with the right Q-content (unique)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.6595em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">row (1,1)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.5795em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:15.659em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-7.5795em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.0795em;\"><span style=\"top:-13.109em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">th</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right