      },
      {
       "data": "Out[158]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{columns G\\_1, G\\_2, G\\_3 are homogeneous of degree 0, -1, -1 for every n} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{det is homogeneous of degree -2} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{Psi\\_B[ns] is homogeneous of degree Total[ns] - 1} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{Psi\\_A[ms] is homogeneous of degree -(Total[ms] + 1)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{=> Psi\\_A[ms] Psi\\_B[ns] has degree Total[ns] - Total[ms] - 2; matching -2 FORCES Total[ns] == Total[ms]} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{CHECK: M[ns,ms] != 0 only if Total[ns] == Total[ms]} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{violations} & \\{\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{nonzero entries per charge sector \\{q, count\\}} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1\\\\1 & 3\\\\2 & 7\\\\3 & 8\\\\4 & 6\\\\5 & 3\\\\6 & 1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{total} & 29\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "c0f1bd96-809f-41d4-87fc-0cb2564233e7"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Charge conservation: `M[ns,ms] != 0` only if `Total[ns] == Total[ms]`\n\nTrue, with zero violations among the 29 entries — and forced, not an accident of the representative.\n\nGrade the sampled values by\n\n$$\\deg\\, Q_i(\\theta_1 + n h) = n, \\qquad \\deg\\, Q^j(\\theta_1 + n h) = -n .$$\n\nThis is nothing but the rescaling of the twist eigenvalues `z -> t z`: the direct `Q_i = z_i^{u/h}P_i` contributes `z_i^n` at the lattice point `n`, and the dual `Q^j = z_j^{-u/h}(...)` contributes `z_j^{-n}`. Under it (all verified symbolically in cell 23):\n\n| object | homogeneous of degree |\n|---|---|\n| the three columns `G_1`, `G_2`, `G_3` | `0`, `-1`, `-1` (uniformly in `n`) |\n| `det N` | `-2` |\n| `Psi_B[ns]` | `Total[ns] - 1` |\n| `Psi_A[ms]` | `-(Total[ms] + 1)` |\n\nThe column grading is the key step: `G_1 = -Q^jQ_i` has degree `n - n = 0`, `G_2 = Q^jQ_i^{[-2]}` has `(n-1) - n = -1`, and `G_3 = Q^{j[2]}Q_i` has `n - (n+1) = -1`, each independent of `n`, so every column is homogeneous and the determinant picks up `0 + (-1) + (-1) = -2`.\n\nTherefore `Psi_A[ms]Psi_B[ns]` has degree `Total[ns] - Total[ms] - 2`, and matching the determinant's `-2` gives\n\n$$\\boxed{\\;\\mathrm{Total}[ns] \\;=\\; \\mathrm{Total}[ms]\\;}$$\n\nThis also settles the uniqueness question of section 5. `det N` is purely of grade `-2`, so any expansion may be projected onto that grade and remains a valid expansion; the projection kills every term with `Total[ns] != Total[ms]`. A representative violating the rule could exist only if its off-grade terms cancelled among themselves — so a charge-conserving representative always exists, and the one `LinearSolve` returned already is one.\n\n**Block structure.** `M` is block diagonal in the total charge `q = Total[ns]`, with\n\n| `q` | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| nonzero entries | 1 | 3 | 7 | 8 | 6 | 3 | 1 |\n\ntotalling 29. The extreme sectors `q = 0` and `q = 6` are one-dimensional, both with `h^6 M = 1/8`, and both diagonal (`{0,0,0} <- {0,0,0}` and `{2,2,2} <- {2,2,2}`).\n\n**Open.** Whether charge conservation plus the block sizes pins `M` down uniquely inside each sector. The `q = 0` and `q = 6` blocks already are unique, being one-dimensional.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. All eight states: two-sided reference normalisation and the functional norm\n\nUse\n[\n\\langle 0|=\\langle 1,0,\\ldots,0|e^{a_{12}E_{12}}e^{a_{13}E_{13}}e^{a_{23}E_{23}},\\qquad\n|0\\rangle=e^{b_{21}E_{21}}e^{b_{31}E_{31}}e^{b_{32}E_{32}}|1,0,\\ldots,0\\rangle .\n]\nFor every common transfer-matrix eigenstate, rescale the right and left eigenvectors so that\n(\\langle0|\\Psi\\rangle=1) and (\\langle\\Psi|0\\rangle=1).  The physical norm is then compared\nwith the functional determinant after dividing by the right reference wave function and by the\nunique dual configuration paired with it on the vacuum.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 17. All common eigenstates and the two exponential reference states. ---- *)\nClearAll[a12, a13, a23, b21, b31, b32, bra0, ket0, seedOp, seedVals,\n  stateR, stateL, stateMu, tEig, commonDiagAll, rightOverlapAll,\n  leftOverlapAll, physicalNormAll];\n\nbra0 = Simplify[{vac} . MatrixExp[a12 EE[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[a13 EE[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[a23 EE[2, 3]]];\nket0 = Simplify[MatrixExp[b21 EE[2, 1]] . MatrixExp[b31 EE[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[b32 EE[3, 2]] . vac];\n\n(* T_1 does not resolve the multiplicity-two weight {1,1,1}; a coefficient of T_2 does. *)\nseedOp = Coefficient[TT[2][u], u, 0];\n{seedVals, stateR} = Eigensystem[seedOp];\nstateR = Transpose[stateR];\nstateL = Inverse[stateR];\nstateMu = Table[\n   Table[FullSimplify[stateL[[s]] . EE[i, i] . stateR[[All, s]]], {i, 3}],\n   {s, dd}];\ntEig[s_, a_] := Expand[stateL[[s]] . TT[a][u] . stateR[[All, s]]];\n\ncommonDiagAll = And @@ Flatten@Table[\n    Module[{mm = Together[stateL . Coefficient[TT[a][u], u, k] . stateR]},\n      Union[Flatten[FullSimplify[mm - DiagonalMatrix[Diagonal[mm]]]]] === {0}],\n    {a, 3}, {k, 0, a}];\n\nrightOverlapAll = Table[Factor[First[bra0] . stateR[[All, s]]], {s, dd}];\nleftOverlapAll = Table[Factor[stateL[[s]] . ket0], {s, dd}];\nphysicalNormAll[s_] := Factor[1/(rightOverlapAll[[s]] leftOverlapAll[[s]])];\n\nGrid[{\n  {\"reference\", \"components in the GT basis\"},\n  {\"<0|\", First[bra0]},\n  {\"|0>\", ket0},\n  {\"all T_a coefficients diagonal in this basis\", commonDiagAll},\n  {\"state weights\", stateMu},\n  {\"vacuum position\", First@FirstPosition[stateMu, {2, 1, 0}]},\n  {\"two-sided normalisation\", \"<Psi|Psi> = 1/(<0|R_Psi> <L_Psi|0>)\"}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"639560\" data-output-id=\"81\" data-out-n=\"172\" data-sub-idx=\"15\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"25\" data-sub-start=\"27\" data-sub-end=\"35\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[172]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"10\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:16.8802em;vertical-align:-8.1701em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.7101em;\"><span style=\"top:-10.6701em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:10.6701em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:16.8402em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-8.1701em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.6701em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.8801em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">reference</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.6801em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&lt;0|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.44em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">|0&gt;</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-11.24em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\