      {
       "data": "Out[242]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{right reference configuration} & \\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\} & {\\square}\\\\\\hline\\text{formal off-shell M-couplings} & \\begin{pmatrix}\\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,0,1\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\}\\end{pmatrix} & {\\square}\\\\\\hline\\text{off-shell coefficient} & \\frac{\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,1\\right)\\,\\left(\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,1\\right)-\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,0\\right)\\right)-\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\left(\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,2\\right)-\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,0\\right)\\right)}{4\\,h^6} & {\\square}\\\\\\hline\\text{boundary Wronskian vanishes for all eight on-shell states} & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\} & {\\square}\\\\\\hline\\text{unique on-shell dual coupling} & \\begin{pmatrix}\\left\\{1,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,0,1\\right\\}\\end{pmatrix} & {\\square}\\\\\\hline\\text{exact on-shell coefficient} & -\\frac{\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\left(\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,2\\right)-\\mathrm{ad}\\left(1,2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{ad}\\left(2,0\\right)\\right)}… [latex truncated: 4166 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "a8499725-926d-4fad-9d53-b4931d8b55b9"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 20. Solve all b parameters in terms of the a parameters. ---- *)\nClearAll[fNormOf, x12Inv, x23Inv, uInv, vInv, z13Inv, z13Branches,\n  alphaConstraints, betaFromAlphaBranches, alphaConstraintRules,\n  betaAlphaChecks, allBranchesMatch];\n\nfNormOf[mu_] := functionalNormAll[First@FirstPosition[stateMu, mu]];\n\n(* Gauge-invariant combinations:\n   X=a12 b21, Y=a23 b32, Z=a13 b31,\n   r=a12 a23/a13, s=b21 b32/b31.\n   The one-dimensional weight sectors determine X,Y,Z(1+r),Z(1-s).\n   The identity r s = X Y/Z gives the two branches for Z. *)\nx12Inv = Factor[1/fNormOf[{1, 2, 0}]];\nx23Inv = Factor[1/fNormOf[{2, 0, 1}]];\nuInv = Factor[(1/fNormOf[{1, 0, 2}])/x23Inv];\nvInv = Factor[(1/fNormOf[{0, 2, 1}])/x12Inv];\n\nz13Branches = Factor[z13Inv /. Solve[\n    Together[(uInv/z13Inv - 1) (1 - vInv/z13Inv)\n      - x12Inv x23Inv/z13Inv] == 0, z13Inv]];\n\n(* All b's are now explicit in the a's.  Since the solution space has only\n   two continuous gauge freedoms, the three a's obey one constraint per branch. *)\nalphaConstraints = Table[Factor[uInv/z13Branches[[q]] - 1],\n   {q, Length[z13Branches]}];\nbetaFromAlphaBranches = Table[\n   {b21 -> Factor[x12Inv/a12],\n    b31 -> Factor[z13Branches[[q]]/a13],\n    b32 -> Factor[x23Inv/a23]},\n   {q, Length[z13Branches]}];\nalphaConstraintRules = Table[\n   a12 -> Factor[alphaConstraints[[q]] a13/a23],\n   {q, Length[z13Branches]}];\n\nbetaAlphaChecks = Table[\n   Table[Factor[Together[\n       ((physicalNormAll[s] /. betaFromAlphaBranches[[q]])\n          /. alphaConstraintRules[[q]]) - functionalNormAll[s]]] === 0,\n     {s, dd}], {q, Length[z13Branches]}];\nallBranchesMatch = And @@ Flatten[betaAlphaChecks];\n\nGrid[{\n  {\"invariant\", \"value fixed by matching\"},\n  {\"a12 b21\", x12Inv},\n  {\"a23 b32\", x23Inv},\n  {\"a13 b31 branches\", z13Branches},\n  {\"branch\", \"constraint on the a's / all b's in terms of the a's\"},\n  {\"I\", Column[Join[\n     {a12 a23/a13 == alphaConstraints[[1]]},\n     betaFromAlphaBranches[[1]]]]},\n  {\"II\", Column[Join[\n     {a12 a23/a13 == alphaConstraints[[2]]},\n     betaFromAlphaBranches[[2]]]]},\n  {\"all eight norms match on each branch\", betaAlphaChecks},\n  {\"MATCH PROVED\", allBranchesMatch}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
