  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result\n\nFor the right reference configuration $(1,0,0)$, treating all sampled Q-values as formally\nindependent first gives the off-shell coefficient\n$$\nc_{\\rm off}[1,0,0]\n=\\frac{\\Psi_A[1,0,0]-\\Psi_A[0,0,1]}{4h^6}.\n$$\nThis is not yet the physical on-shell answer. Every one of the eight dual Baxter solutions obeys\nthe boundary Wronskian identity\n$$\nQ^1(\\theta)Q^2(\\theta+h)-Q^2(\\theta)Q^1(\\theta+h)=0,\n$$\nand hence\n$$\n\\Psi_A[1,0,0]=\nQ^1(\\theta+h)\n\\bigl[Q^1(\\theta)Q^2(\\theta+h)-Q^2(\\theta)Q^1(\\theta+h)\\bigr]=0.\n$$\nTherefore the exact on-shell coefficient has exactly one dual configuration:\n$$\n\\boxed{c[1,0,0]=\n-\\frac{\\Psi_A[0,0,1]}{4h^6}}\n$$\nwith\n$$\n\\Psi_A[0,0,1]=\nQ^1(\\theta)\n\\bigl[Q^1(\\theta)Q^2(\\theta+2h)-Q^2(\\theta)Q^1(\\theta+2h)\\bigr].\n$$\nThe functional norm is consequently\n$$\n\\widehat N_s=C_{\\rm vac}\\,\n\\frac{\\det N_s}{\\Psi_{A,s}[0,0,1]\\,\\Psi_{B,s}[1,0,0]},\n$$\nwith the overall constant fixed by the vacuum norm.\n\nAll $b$ parameters can be written in terms of the $a$ parameters:\n$$\nb_{21}=-\\frac{z_1(z_1-z_3)}{a_{12}z_2(z_2-z_3)},\\qquad\nb_{32}=-\\frac{z_2^2(z_1-z_3)}\n {a_{23}(z_1-z_2)z_3^2}.\n$$\nThere are two branches for $b_{31}$, accompanied by one constraint on the three $a$'s:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{I:}\\quad&\nb_{31}=-\\frac{z_1^2}{a_{13}z_3^2},&\n\\frac{a_{12}a_{23}}{a_{13}}\n&=-\\frac{z_2(z_1-z_3)}{z_1(z_2-z_3)},\\\\[1mm]\n\\text{II:}\\quad&\nb_{31}=-\\frac{z_1}{a_{13}z_3},&\n\\frac{a_{12}a_{23}}{a_{13}}\n&=-\\frac{z_1-z_3}{z_2-z_3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBoth branches reproduce all eight functional norms.",
